BE-300 2.6.8.1: keep VR41xx clear_page/copy_page on 32-bit loads/stores.

VR41xx is MIPS III, so the generic probe reports a 64-bit zero register
and pg-r4k.c generates sd/ld page operations even for this 32-bit kernel.
The BE-300 emulator executes 32-bit instructions only (same constraint as
the 4.2.9 port's clear_word_size/copy_word_size = 4), so the new
mach-vr41xx/cpu-feature-overrides.h turns the 64-bit register features
off for CONFIG_MIPS32.

---
 .../mach-vr41xx/cpu-feature-overrides.h       | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 include/asm-mips/mach-vr41xx/cpu-feature-overrides.h

diff --git a/include/asm-mips/mach-vr41xx/cpu-feature-overrides.h b/include/asm-mips/mach-vr41xx/cpu-feature-overrides.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..35d503ed62cd0223215fa96ba3dac2bd01097f99
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/asm-mips/mach-vr41xx/cpu-feature-overrides.h
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+/*
+ * NEC VR41xx CPU feature overrides.
+ *
+ * The VR41xx cores are MIPS III, so the generic probe reports a 64-bit
+ * zero register and the dynamically generated clear_page/copy_page in
+ * arch/mips/mm/pg-r4k.c use sd/ld.  This port runs a 32-bit kernel, and
+ * the BE-300 emulator executes 32-bit instructions only (the same
+ * constraint as the Linux 4.2.9 port's clear_word_size/copy_word_size = 4),
+ * so keep every generated page operation on lw/sw.
+ *
+ * This file is subject to the terms and conditions of the GNU General Public
+ * License.  See the file "COPYING" in the main directory of this archive
+ * for more details.
+ */
+#ifndef __ASM_MACH_VR41XX_CPU_FEATURE_OVERRIDES_H
+#define __ASM_MACH_VR41XX_CPU_FEATURE_OVERRIDES_H
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_MIPS32
+#define cpu_has_64bit_zero_reg		0
+#define cpu_has_64bit_gp_regs		0
+#define cpu_has_64bit_addresses		0
+#endif
+
+#endif /* __ASM_MACH_VR41XX_CPU_FEATURE_OVERRIDES_H */
